**In Nevada, the deadline is 30 days.** After the lease ends and the tenant moves out, the landlord has 30 days to either return the deposit or send a written, itemized list of deductions.

Other Nevada rules from the same guide:
- **Maximum deposit:** 3 months' rent. This counts all security together, including any surety bond and prepaid last month's rent.
- **Penalty for missing the deadline:** The landlord can owe the whole deposit, plus up to that same amount again in damages set by a court. That's up to 2x the deposit.
- **Move-in record:** Every written lease must provide for a signed list of what's in the unit and its condition. Photos aren't required.

**Source:** [PropInspect – Nevada Security Deposit Laws](https://propinspect.net/security-deposit-laws/nevada), last reviewed October 12, 2026, based on [NRS § 118A.242](https://www.leg.state.nv.us/NRS/NRS-118A.html#NRS118ASec242).

